"visdat\":{\"31bf38e548ea\":[\"function (y) \",\"x\"],\"31bf551617d4\":[\"function (y) \",\"x\"]},\"highlight\":{\"on\":\"plotly_click\",\"persistent\":false,\"dynamic\":false,\"selectize\":false,\"opacityDim\":0.20000000000000001,\"selected\":{\"opacity\":1},\"debounce\":0},\"shinyEvents\":[\"plotly_hover\",\"plotly_click\",\"plotly_selected\",\"plotly_relayout\",\"plotly_brushed\",\"plotly_brushing\",\"plotly_clickannotation\",\"plotly_doubleclick\",\"plotly_deselect\",\"plotly_afterplot\",\"plotly_sunburstclick\"],\"base_url\":\"https://plot.ly\"},\"evals\":[],\"jsHooks\":[]}</script>\n```\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## Line Chart Example\n\n<br>\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](week-2.2_files/figure-revealjs/geom_line1-1.png){width=960}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n##\n\n<br>\n\nHere is the code... \n\n<br>\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\n# in this ggplot() call, we add a third dimension for line color\nggplot(dem_waves_ctrs, aes(x = year, y = polyarchy, color = country)) +\n  geom_line(linewidth = 1) + # our geom is a line with a width of 1\n  labs(\n    x = \"Year\", \n    y = \"Polyarchy Score\", \n    title = 'Democracy in countries representing three different \"waves\"', \n    caption = \"Source: V-Dem Institute\", \n    color = \"Country\" # make title of legend to upper case\n  )\n```\n:::\n\n\n## \n\n<br>\n\nUse `geom_line()` to specify a line chart... \n\n<br>\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code  code-line-numbers=\"3\"}\n# in this ggplot() call, we add a third dimension for line color\nggplot(dem_waves_ctrs, aes(x = year, y = polyarchy, color = country)) +\n  geom_line(linewidth = 1) + # our geom is a line with a width of 1\n  labs(\n    x = \"Year\", \n    y = \"Polyarchy Score\", \n    title = 'Democracy in countries representing three different \"waves\"', \n    caption = \"Source: V-Dem Institute\", \n    color = \"Country\" # make title of legend to upper case\n  )\n```\n:::\n\n\n## \n\n<br>\n\nAdd third dimension to the `aes()` call for line color...\n\n<br>\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code  code-line-numbers=\"2\"}\n# in this ggplot() call, we add a third dimension for line color\nggplot(dem_waves_ctrs, aes(x = year, y = polyarchy, color = country)) +\n  geom_line(linewidth = 1) + # our geom is a line with a width of 1\n  labs(\n    x = \"Year\", \n    y = \"Polyarchy Score\", \n    title = 'Democracy in countries representing three different \"waves\"', \n    caption = \"Source: V-Dem Institute\", \n    color = \"Country\" # make title of legend to upper case\n  )\n```\n:::\n\n\n## \n\n<br>\n\nModify the legend title...\n\n<br>\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code  code-line-numbers=\"9\"}\n# in this ggplot() call, we add a third dimension for line color\nggplot(dem_waves_ctrs, aes(x = year, y = polyarchy, color = country)) +\n  geom_line(linewidth = 1) + # our geom is a line with a width of 1\n  labs(\n    x = \"Year\", \n    y = \"Polyarchy Score\", \n    title = 'Democracy in countries representing three different \"waves\"', \n    caption = \"Source: V-Dem Institute\", \n    color = \"Country\" # make title of legend to upper case\n  )\n```\n:::\n\n\n## Your Turn!\n\n<br>\n\n- See table three of [this article](https://kurzman.unc.edu/wp-content/uploads/sites/1410/2011/06/Kurzman_Waves_of_Democratization.pdf)\n- Select three countries to visualize\n- Adjust setup code to filter data on those countries \n- Visualize with `geom_line()`\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<countdown-timer class=\"countdown\" id=\"timer1\" minutes=\"10\" seconds=\"0\" update-every=\"1\" tabindex=\"0\" style=\"right:10%;bottom:10%;--countdown-color-border:#fff;--countdown-color-text:#fff;--countdown-color-running-background:#42affa;--countdown-color-running-text:black;--countdown-color-finished-background:#E5D19D;--countdown-color-finished-text:#00264A;\"></countdown-timer>\n```\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## Scatter Plots\n\n<br>\n\n- Scatter plots are used to show the relationship between two variables\n- Frequently the outcome variable is on the y-axis and the predictor variable is on the x-axis\n- In addition to the points, you can use color, size, and shape to add more information to the plot\n\n## Scatter Plot Setup\n\n<br>\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\ndem_summary_ctry <- read_csv(\"data/dem_women.csv\") |>\n  group_by(country, region) |> # group by country, keep region\n  summarize(\n    polyarchy = mean(polyarchy, na.rm = TRUE),\n    gdp_pc = mean(gdp_pc, na.rm = TRUE), \n    flfp = mean(flfp, na.rm = TRUE), \n    women_rep = mean(women_rep, na.rm = TRUE)\n  )\n```\n:::\n\n\n## Scatter Plot\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code  code-fold=\"true\"}\nggplot(dem_summary_ctry, aes(x = gdp_pc, y = polyarchy, color = region, size = women_rep)) + \n  geom_point() + # use geom_point() for scatter plots\n  scale_x_log10(labels = scales::label_number(prefix = \"$\", suffix = \"k\")) +\n  labs(\n    x= \"GDP per Capita\", \n    y = \"Polyarchy Score\",\n    title = \"Wealth and democracy, 1990 - present\", \n    caption = \"Source: V-Dem Institute\", \n    color = \"Region\",\n    size = \"Women Reps\"\n    ) \n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](week-2.2_files/figure-revealjs/scatter1-1.png){width=960}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## Scatter Plot\n\n<br>\n\nUse `geom_point()`...\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code  code-line-numbers=\"2\"}\nggplot(dem_summary_ctry, aes(x = gdp_pc, y = polyarchy, color = region, size = women_rep)) +\n  geom_point() + # use geom_point() for scatter plots\n  scale_x_log10(labels = scales::label_number(prefix = \"$\", suffix = \"k\")) +\n  labs(\n    x= \"GDP per Capita\", \n    y = \"Polyarchy Score\",\n    title = \"Wealth and democracy, 1990 - present\", \n    caption = \"Source: V-Dem Institute\", \n    color = \"Region\",\n    size = \"Women Reps\"\n    ) \n```\n:::\n\n\n## Scatter Plot\n\n<br>\n\nFour dimensions... \n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code  code-line-numbers=\"1-1\"}\nggplot(dem_summary_ctry, aes(x = gdp_pc, y = polyarchy, color = region, size = women_rep)) + \n  geom_point() + # use geom_point() for scatter plots\n  scale_x_log10(labels = scales::label_number(prefix = \"$\", suffix = \"k\")) +\n  labs(\n    x= \"GDP per Capita\", \n    y = \"Polyarchy Score\",\n    title = \"Wealth and democracy, 1990 - present\", \n    caption = \"Source: V-Dem Institute\", \n    color = \"Region\",\n    size = \"Women Reps\"\n    ) \n```\n:::\n\n\n## Scatter Plot\n\n<br>\n\nStretch axis on log scale and use `scales` package to adjust labels...\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code  code-line-numbers=\"3\"}\nggplot(dem_summary_ctry, aes(x = gdp_pc, y = polyarchy, color = region, size = women_rep)) + \n  geom_point() + # use geom_point() for scatter plots\n  scale_x_log10(labels = scales::label_number(prefix = \"$\", suffix = \"k\")) +\n  labs(\n    x= \"GDP per Capita\", \n    y = \"Polyarchy Score\",\n    title = \"Wealth and democracy, 1990 - present\", \n    caption = \"Source: V-Dem Institute\", \n    color = \"Region\",\n    size = \"Women Reps\"\n    ) \n```\n:::\n\n\n\n## Scatter Plot\n\n<br>\n\nChange legend titles... \n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code  code-line-numbers=\"9-10\"}\nggplot(dem_summary_ctry, aes(x = gdp_pc, y = polyarchy, color = region, size = women_rep)) + \n  geom_point() + # use geom_point() for scatter plots\n  scale_x_log10(labels = scales::label_number(prefix = \"$\", suffix = \"k\")) +\n  labs(\n    x= \"GDP per Capita\", \n    y = \"Polyarchy Score\",\n    title = \"Wealth and democracy, 1990 - present\", \n    caption = \"Source: V-Dem Institute\", \n    color = \"Region\",\n    size = \"Women Reps\"\n    ) \n```\n:::\n\n\n## Your Turn! \n\n- There are four variables in `dem_summary_ctry`\n- Pick one related to women's empowerment\n- Visualize it on the y-axis with `gdp_pc` or `polyarchy` on the x-axis \n- Change labels and legend titles to match your visualization\n- Interpret your plot\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<countdown-timer class=\"countdown\" id=\"women_emp\" minutes=\"10\" seconds=\"0\" update-every=\"1\" tabindex=\"0\" style=\"right:0;bottom:0;\"></countdown-timer>\n```\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## Add a Trend Line\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](week-2.2_files/figure-revealjs/trend_line1-1.png){width=960}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## Add a Trend Line\n\n<br>\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code  code-line-numbers=\"3\"}\nggplot(dem_summary_ctry, aes(x = gdp_pc, y = polyarchy)) + \n  geom_point(aes(color = region)) + \n  geom_smooth(method = \"lm\", linewidth = 1) + \n  scale_x_log10(labels = scales::label_number(prefix = \"$\", suffix = \"k\")) +\n  labs(\n    x= \"GDP per Capita\", \n    y = \"Polyarchy Score\",\n    title = \"Wealth and democracy, 1990 - present\", \n    caption = \"Source: V-Dem Institute\", \n    color = \"Region\"\n    ) \n```\n:::\n\n\n## Add a Trend Line\n\n<br>\n\nTaking out size and adding color to `geom_point()` call...\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code  code-line-numbers=\"1-2\"}\nggplot(dem_summary_ctry, aes(x = gdp_pc, y = polyarchy)) + \n  geom_point(aes(color = region)) + \n  geom_smooth(method = \"lm\", linewidth = 1) + \n  scale_x_log10(labels = scales::label_number(prefix = \"$\", suffix = \"k\")) +\n  labs(\n    x= \"GDP per Capita\", \n    y = \"Polyarchy Score\",\n    title = \"Wealth and democracy, 1990 - present\", \n    caption = \"Source: V-Dem Institute\", \n    color = \"Region\"\n    ) \n```\n:::\n\n\n## Add a Trend Line\n\n<br>\n\nChanging legend titles...\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code  code-line-numbers=\"5-11\"}\nggplot(dem_summary_ctry, aes(x = gdp_pc, y = polyarchy)) + \n  geom_point(aes(color = region)) + \n  geom_smooth(method = \"lm\", linewidth = 1) + \n  scale_x_log10(labels = scales::label_number(prefix = \"$\", suffix = \"k\")) +\n  labs(\n    x= \"GDP per Capita\", \n    y = \"Polyarchy Score\",\n    title = \"Wealth and democracy, 1990 - present\", \n    caption = \"Source: V-Dem Institute\", \n    color = \"Region\"\n    ) \n```\n:::\n\n\n## Your Turn! \n\n<br>\n\n- Add a trendline to your plot\n- Change the labels accordingly\n- Try using `method = \"loess\"` instead of a \"lm\"\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<countdown-timer class=\"countdown\" id=\"timer2\" minutes=\"10\" seconds=\"0\" update-every=\"1\" tabindex=\"0\" style=\"right:10%;bottom:10%;\"></countdown-timer>\n```\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## Which Plot Should You Use? \n\n<br>\n\n:::{.incremental}\n- Trends in stock process over time\n- Distribution of income in a country\n- Comparison of FLFP across MENA countries\n- Relationship between poverty and inequality (cross-nationally)\n:::\n\n## Which Geom Would You Use?\n\n<br>\n\n:::{.incremental}\n- Column chart\n- Histogram\n- Line chart\n- Scatter plot\n:::\n\n## Other Plots and Geometries {.smaller}\n\n<br>\n\n:::{.columns}\n::::{.column width=50%}\n- **Box Plot**  \n  `geom_boxplot()`\n  \n- **Violin Plot**  \n  `geom_violin()`\n  \n- **Density Plot**  \n  `geom_density()`\n  \n- **Bar Plot (Categorical)**  \n  `geom_bar()`\n  \n- **Heatmap**  \n  `geom_tile()`\n::::\n\n::::{.column width=50%}\n- **Area Plot**  \n  `geom_area()`\n  \n- **Dot Plot**  \n  `geom_dotplot()`\n  \n- **Pie Chart**  \n  (usually a bar plot with `coord_polar()`)\n\n- **Ridgeline Plot**  \n  `ggridges::geom_density_ridges()`\n  \n- **Map Plot (Choropleth)**  \n  `geom_polygon()`\n::::\n:::\n\n\n",
